      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Huh... This may actually extend to worlds as well. In a world I'm working on, sometimes when looking in very specific directions the CPU time will spike in the exact same way as in the video, also creating the sawtooth-like pattern in the frametime chart. I have nothing that is view dependent that would cause this, but I *do* have occlusion culling set up... I wonder if this is a related issue.\nI have a 1070Ti and a Ryzen 3950x.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
